+# FlyWeb: release after 3.2.2 (softmac `seguridad/siguiente-3`), V8 fix 7ef85e6153 (crbug 587040688)
+
+SEGURIDAD-PORTES-33, 25-11-2026 (softmac `FlyWeb/seguridad/siguiente-3/brave-core/0009`). V8 15.6 7ef85e6153
+(15.6.75.85, 25-11; bugs 588740578 and 587040688; cherry-pick of main b9c28af54c). Applied as is to 15.6.75.66.
+Severity not published.
+
+- When a loop backedge died in the middle of `PrePhiUntaggingPhase`, later uses and deopt frames unwrapped the
+  1-input Phi to its input while earlier uses still pointed at the Phi. `MaglevPhiRepresentationSelector` could then
+  untag (truncate or unbox) that Phi inconsistently with its unwrapped uses: a JIT miscompile, the classic path to
+  type confusion. Single-input Phis now stay tagged.
+- `maglev-phi-representation-selector.cc` is not touched by any other `patches/v8` file. Maglev is on by default
+  in 156, so this is reachable from any page.
+
+**Cache epoch:** covered by the single 40 -> 41 bump of `siguiente-3` (`brave-core/0001`); no bytecode change.
+
+To check (D8-LINUX): mjsunit `turbolev/regress-587040688` (`--turbolev`), `maglev/*` and `turbolev/*`, with and
+without `--maglev`.
+
 # FlyWeb: release after 3.2.2 (softmac `seguridad/siguiente-3`), V8 fix d76136bcef (crbug 589433702), ported from the M159 merge
 
 SEGURIDAD-PORTES-33, 25-11-2026 (softmac `FlyWeb/seguridad/siguiente-3/brave-core/0008`). **Not merged to 15.6
diff --git a/patches/v8/src-maglev-maglev-phi-representation-selector.cc.patch b/patches/v8/src-maglev-maglev-phi-representation-selector.cc.patch
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..64282d3d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/patches/v8/src-maglev-maglev-phi-representation-selector.cc.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+diff --git a/src/maglev/maglev-phi-representation-selector.cc b/src/maglev/maglev-phi-representation-selector.cc
+index 5b44744d9e9517e13de2f6a2fb5f82259475c24e..1e672736354ca0d07a1508fc641ccc229f61c14a 100644
+--- a/src/maglev/maglev-phi-representation-selector.cc
++++ b/src/maglev/maglev-phi-representation-selector.cc
+@@ -143,6 +143,14 @@ MaglevPhiRepresentationSelector::ProcessPhi(Phi* node) {
+     return ProcessPhiResult::kNone;
+   }
+ 
++  if (node->input_count() == 1) {
++    // Later passes unwrap single-input Phis to their input, so uses/deopt
++    // frames may already bypass this Phi while earlier uses still point to it.
++    // Keep it tagged so its representation cannot diverge from its input's.
++    EnsurePhiInputsTagged(node);
++    return ProcessPhiResult::kNone;
++  }
++
+   TRACE_UNTAGGING("Considering for untagging: " << PrintNodeLabel(node));
+ 
+   // {input_mask} represents the ValueRepresentation that {node} could have,
diff --git a/patches/v8/test-mjsunit-turbolev-regress-587040688.js.patch b/patches/v8/test-mjsunit-turbolev-regress-587040688.js.patch
